{{!--
  Spike for the view modularisation (issue #9 preparation).

  Proves that Handlebars PARTIALS resolve for a MeshCentral plugin view. Verified against the upstream
  source: pluginHandler.handleAdminReq does `serv.app.set('views', <pluginPath>/<pin>/views)` before
  calling the plugin, and webserver.js creates the engine with `exphbs.engine({ defaultLayout: false })`
  - no partialsDir. express-handlebars@8 derives it PER RENDER from the views path Express resolved:
  `this.partialsDir = this.config.partialsDir || path.join(viewsPath, "partials/")`, and `_getDir` globs
  `**/*.handlebars` with posix paths, so sub-folders become namespaces
  (views/partials/panels/x.handlebars => `{{> panels/x }}`).

  This marker is asserted locally by tools/test-views.js and - the actual point of the spike - live by
  the CI container test against a real MeshCentral server. It renders as an HTML comment, so the panel
  looks exactly as before.
--}}
